From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 23:38:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: samsung: exynos-pmu: drop the gs201 compatible

gs201's PMU now carries google,gs101-pmu as a fallback, as the binding
documents, and that entry has the same data. This reverts commit
02d0019a7661 ("soc: samsung: exynos-pmu: add Google gs201 compatible").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c b/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c
index 85056d540..b13a93f09 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c
@@ -126,9 +126,6 @@ static const struct of_device_id exynos_pmu_of_device_ids[] = {
 	{
 		.compatible = "google,gs101-pmu",
 		.data = &gs101_pmu_data,
-	}, {
-		.compatible = "google,gs201-pmu",
-		.data = &gs101_pmu_data,
 	}, {
 		.compatible = "google,zuma-pmu",
 		.data = &zuma_pmu_data,
